.TH GFP-PUSH 1 "September 2026" "gfp-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfp-push \- Submit changelist to the Perforce depot (via Jenkins gated submit queue or direct submit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfp push
[\fB\-c\fR \fICL\fR | \fB\-\-cl\fR \fICL\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR | \fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR | \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-gated\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfp push
translates the standard Git push mental model into Perforce changelist submissions.

Perforce utilizes an atomic changelist submission model (\fBp4 submit\fR). In enterprise environments, directly submitting untested changes to mainline streams can break builds. To maintain continuous mainline stability,
.B gfp push
supports a dual-submission architecture:

.SS 1. Gated Submit Queue (Default)
In gated mode (the default),
.B gfp push
shelves the pending changelist (\fBp4 shelve\fR) onto the Perforce server and notifies the CI server (e.g. Jenkins). The automated pipeline unshelves the changelist into an isolated test environment, runs linters and test suites, and, upon successful verification, submits the changelist atomically to the depot (\fBp4 submit \-e\fR) on behalf of the developer via a service bot.

The submit queue URL is configured via \fBGFP_SUBMIT_QUEUE_URL\fR or the \fBsubmit_queue_url\fR setting in \fB.gfp/config.json\fR.

.SS 2. Direct Force Submission (\-f, \-\-force)
Passing
.B \-f
or
.B \-\-force
bypasses the Jenkins gated submit queue and directly submits the changelist to the depot (\fBp4 submit\fR). This is equivalent to standard Perforce submission or \fBgit push\fR to a repository without pre-receive branch protection.

.SS Automatic Changelist Discovery
If
.BR \-c " / " \-\-cl
is omitted,
.B gfp push
automatically locates the most recent pending changelist owned by the active Perforce client workspace and user.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Specific pending changelist ID to submit. If omitted,
.B gfp
targets the most recent pending changelist.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force direct submission to the depot (\fBp4 submit\fR), bypassing the Jenkins gated submit queue.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Simulate the push operation. Displays whether changes would be shelved for the gated queue or force-submitted directly, and lists all files contained within the target changelist.
.TP
.B \-\-gated
Explicitly request submission via the Jenkins gated submit queue. This is the default push behavior.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B GFP_SUBMIT_QUEUE_URL
The HTTP or HTTPS URL of the Jenkins gated submit queue validation job.
.TP
.B GFP_PUSH_MODE
Default push behavior (\fBgated\fR or \fBdirect\fR).
.TP
.B P4PORT
Perforce server address.
.TP
.B P4USER
Perforce user name.
.TP
.B P4CLIENT
Perforce client workspace name.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration options may be placed in \fB.gfp/config.json\fR (workspace-scoped) or \fB~/.gfp/config.json\fR (user-scoped):
.PP
.nf
{
    "submit_queue_url": "http://jenkins.corp.local/job/gfp-submit-queue/",
    "push_mode": "gated"
}
.fi

.SH LIFECYCLE HOOKS
.TP
.BR pre\-push ", " pre_push
Executed immediately before shelving or submitting the changelist. If the hook exits with a non-zero status, submission is aborted.
.TP
.BR post\-push ", " post_push
Executed after the changelist has been successfully shelved (gated queue) or submitted (direct mode).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Submit current pending changelist via the gated submit queue:
.nf
$ gfp push
.fi

.TP
.B Dry run preview of what would be submitted:
.nf
$ gfp push -n
.fi

.TP
.B Force direct submission of a specific changelist to depot:
.nf
$ gfp push -f -c 12345
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gfp (1),
.BR gfp\-commit (1),
.BR p4 (1),
.BR git\-push (1)
